# Avatar Canvas Safety Rules

## CRITICAL: Incident History

This project has suffered **repeated black-screen / avatar-disappear** incidents from:
1. `null.addEventListener` — Canvas mounted before outer div was in DOM (React 19 + Turbopack async configure)
2. Static import of VRMAPlayer caused Turbopack build failure → black screen
3. VRM model path 404 (`cogni.vrm` missing) → silent load failure → empty canvas

## NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

### Rule 1 — Canvas Mount Guard (NEVER remove)
`AvatarCanvas.tsx` MUST keep this exact pattern:
```tsx
const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const [domReady, setDomReady] = useState(false);
useEffect(() => { setDomReady(true); }, []);
// ...
<div ref={containerRef}>
  {domReady && <Canvas eventSource={containerRef as React.RefObject<HTMLElement>}>
```
- `domReady` gate ensures Canvas never mounts before DOM is ready
- `useRef` not `useState` for the container (avoids re-render race)
- `useEffect` runs only after DOM insert — guaranteed non-null

### Rule 2 — VRMAPlayer (NEVER static import)
```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — causes Turbopack build failure → black screen
import { VRMAPlayer } from './VRMAPlayer';

// ✅ REQUIRED — dynamic import with catch, avatar renders even if VRMA fails
const VRMAPlayerDynamic = dynamic(
  () => import('./VRMAPlayer')
    .then((m) => ({ default: m.VRMAPlayer }))
    .catch(() => ({ default: () => null })),
  { ssr: false },
);
```

### Rule 3 — VRM Fallback Chain (NEVER remove)
```tsx
// Always try multiple paths; never fail hard on single URL
const loadChain = [vrmUrl, ...VRM_FALLBACKS, '/models/avaturn_avatar.vrm', '/models/cogni.vrm']
  .filter(Boolean)
  .filter((u, i, arr) => arr.indexOf(u) === i);
// tryLoadAt(0) tries each in order on failure
```

### Rule 4 — Primary VRM URL
- `.env.local`: `NEXT_PUBLIC_AVATAR_VRM_URL=/models/avaturn_avatar.vrm`
- `/models/cogni.vrm` is **404** on this machine — DO NOT set as primary
- `/models/avaturn_avatar.vrm` returns **200** — always use this

## MANDATORY PRE-CHECK (before any avatar edit)

Run and confirm ALL of these before starting:
```
1. HTTP /models/avaturn_avatar.vrm → 200 ✅
2. HTTP /models/cogni.vrm → may be 404 (not primary)
3. AvatarCanvas.tsx contains: domReady gate, containerRef, VRMAPlayerDynamic
4. NEXT_PUBLIC_AVATAR_VRM_URL=/models/avaturn_avatar.vrm in .env.local
```

## SAFE CHANGE PROTOCOL

1. Make ONE file change at a time
2. Run `npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck` — must pass
3. Confirm avatar visible (no black screen) before next change
4. If avatar disappears: immediately revert last change, report exact console error

## ROLLBACK COMMAND

```bash
git checkout HEAD -- frontend/src/app/avatar-agent/AvatarCanvas.tsx
```

## SCOPE LIMITS

When editing avatar files, DO NOT also change:
- `next.config.js` transpilePackages
- `package.json` dependencies
- Other unrelated features

One concern per PR/session.
